
#brick

%% (explosion in $Container) is dispatched when the fuse burns down.
%% The dispatch is deferred to (late on every tick) because setting a
%% new (timer running) fact from inside the timer exhaust loop makes the
%% exhaust re-enumerate it and count it down to zero in the same pass.
(interface (explosion in $>Container))
(interface (explosion pending in $>Container))
%% Marks a room whose delayed collapse fuse (SAFE-MUNG) is ticking.
%% The (on $room timeout) rules below also see EVERY object timeout
%% (matchbook fuses, knockouts...), so they must be guarded by this.
(interface ($<Room collapsing))

~(unlikely [tie #wire-coil to #brick])

(instead of [put $obj #in *])
	(try [tie $obj to *])

(perform [tie #wire-coil to *])
	You insert the wire coil into the brick.
	(now) (#wire-coil is #tiedto *)

(on #wire-coil timeout)
    (#brick has parent $container)
    (now) (#brick is nowhere)
    (now) (explosion pending in $container)

(late on every tick)
    (explosion pending in $container)
    (now) ~(explosion pending in $container)
    (explosion in $container)

%% Player at the blast site (brick's parent is the current room, or the
%% player holds the brick): FUSE-FUNCTION's <==? .BRICK-ROOM ,HERE> branch,
%% <JIGS-UP ,BRICK-BOOM>.
(explosion in $container)
    { (current room $container) (or) (current player $container) }
    Now you've done it.  It seems that the brick has other properties
    than weight, namely the ability to blow you to smithereens.
    (jigs up)

%% Brick in the hole of the rusty box: the safe opens (original SAFE
%% branch of FUSE-FUNCTION).  No death - the delayed collapse fuse below
%% handles the consequences.
(explosion in #hole)
    (#hole is in room $room)
    (now) ~(#box is closed)
    (now) (#hole is nowhere)
    (now) (collapsing $room)
    (now) ($room timer is 5)
    (now) ($room timer running)
    (narrate explosion in room $room)

%% Explosion somewhere else: SAFE-MUNG is registered 5 turns out
%% (<CLOCK-INT ,SAFIN 5>); it kills anyone still in the room then.
(explosion in $container)
    ($container is in room $room)
    (now) (collapsing $room)
    (now) ($room timer is 5)
    (now) ($room timer running)
    (narrate explosion in room $room)

%% Same, when the brick's parent is a room itself.
(explosion in $container)
    (now) (collapsing $container)
    (now) ($container timer is 5)
    (now) ($container timer running)
    (narrate explosion in room $container)

%% The original TELLs this unconditionally (no adjacency check).
(narrate explosion in room $room)
    There is an explosion nearby.

%% SAFE-MUNG, 5 turns after an explosion away from the player.
(on $room timeout)
    (collapsing $room)
    (current room $room)
    (if) ($room is in the house) (then)
		The house shakes, and the ceiling of the room you're in collapses,
		turning you into a pancake.
	(else)
		The room trembles and 50,000 pounds of rock fall on you, turning you
		into a pancake.
	(endif)
    (jigs up)

(on $room timeout)
    (collapsing $room)
    (now) ($room has been munged)
    You may recall your recent explosion.  Well, probably as a result of
    that, you hear an ominous rumbling, as if one of the rooms in the
    dungeon had collapsed.

%% MUNG-ROOM blocks the exits of the munged room (leaving it; entering
%% from the wide ledge is blocked in volcano.dg).
(prevent [leave $room $dir])
    ($room has been munged)
    The way is blocked by debris from an explosion.

%%%

%% SAFE
#dusty-room
(room *)
(name *)	Dusty Room
(look *)
	You are in a dusty old room which is virtually featureless, except
	for an exit on the north side.
	(par)
	(if) (#box is closed) (then)
		Imbedded in the far wall, there is a rusty old box.  It appears that
		the box is somewhat damaged, since an oblong hole has been chipped
		out of the front of it.
		(list contents of #hole)
	(else)
		On the far wall is a rusty box, whose door has been blown off.
		(list contents of #box)
	(endif)
%% TODO: room action routine SAFE-ROOM
(from * go #north to #wide-ledge)

%% FUSE
#wire-coil
(* is #in #stream)
(name *)	wire coil
(item *)
(flammable *)
(dict *)	shiny thin fuse
(* size is 1)
(appearance *)
	There is a coil of thin shiny wire here.
%% TODO: object action routine FUSE-FUNCTION
(* timer is 2)

%% BRICK
#brick
(* is #in #attic)
(name *)	brick
(item *)
(flammable *)
(dict *)	square clay
(* size is 9)
(* capacity is 2)
(appearance *)
	There is a square brick here which feels like clay.
(descr *)
	The brick is square and soft like clay.
	(list contents of *)

%% SAFE
#box
(* is #in #dusty-room)
(name *)	box
(container *)
(* is closed)
(dict *)	safe
(* capacity is 15)

(prevent [take *])
    The box is imbedded in the wall.
(prevent [open/close *])
	~(* is closed)
	The box has no door!
(prevent [open *])
	(* is closed)
	The box is rusted and will not open.
(prevent [close *])
	(* is closed)
	The box is not open, chomper!

(grammar [blast/explode/detonate [object]] for [blast $])
(grammar [blow up [object]] for [blast $])
(prevent [blast *])
	What do you expect, BOOM?

%% CARD
#card
(* is #in #box)
(name *)	card
(item *)
(readable *)
(flammable *)
(dict *)	note card
(* size is 1)
(appearance *)
	There is a card with writing on it here.
(descr *)
	Warning:(line)
	This room was constructed over very weak rock strata.
	Detonation of explosives in this room is strictly prohibited!
	(div @right) { Frobozz Magic Cave Company(line)per M. Agrippa, foreman }

%% SSLOT
#hole
(* is #in #dusty-room)
(name *)	hole
(dict *)	slot
(container *)
(* capacity is 10)

